sequenceDiagram
    actor C as Client
    participant O as OVS switch
    participant S as SDN controller
    participant E as Edge server
    participant D as Storage member<br/>(MongoDB)

    Note over C,D: VIP_SERVER — service routing surface
    C->>O: 1 · HTTP request to VIP_SERVER
    Note right of O: no flow rule → punt to controller
    O->>S: 2 · Packet-In (first packet)
    S->>S: 3 · select_server():<br/>lowest WSM cost over the edge pool
    S->>O: 4 · install DNAT / SNAT rules
    O->>E: 5 · forwarded to the selected edge server

    Note over C,D: VIP_DATA — data routing surface
    E->>O: 6 · MongoDB query to VIP_DATA
    Note right of O: no flow rule → punt to controller
    O->>S: 7 · Packet-In (first packet)
    S->>S: 8 · select_storage():<br/>lowest WSM cost over the replica set
    S->>O: 9 · install DNAT rules
    O->>D: 10 · forwarded to the selected member

    D-->>O: result (SNAT rewrites member → VIP_DATA)
    O-->>E: response
    E-->>O: response (SNAT rewrites edge → VIP_SERVER)
    O-->>C: response

    Note over C,D: return path: SNAT rules rewrite backend addresses back to the virtual addresses,<br/>so clients and replicas never learn backend identities
    Note over C,D: flow-based forwarding: subsequent packets of the same flow are handled in the data plane,<br/>without controller intervention
